    "answer": {
      "short": "$x\\approx6.5$, $y\\approx5.3$.",
      "worked": "$A$, $D$ and $C$ lie on a straight line.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle ADB&=180^\\circ-50^\\circ\\\\\\angle ADB&=130^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\n\nUse the sine rule in $\\triangle ADB$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x}{\\sin30^\\circ}&=\\frac{10}{\\sin130^\\circ}\\\\x&=\\frac{10\\sin30^\\circ}{\\sin130^\\circ}\\\\x&\\approx6.5\\end{align*}$$\n\nUse the sine rule in $\\triangle ABC$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{y}{\\sin30^\\circ}&=\\frac{10}{\\sin70^\\circ}\\\\y&=\\frac{10\\sin30^\\circ}{\\sin70^\\circ}\\\\y&\\approx5.3\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
